 "description": "One format as a creator shoots it: its plan, its hits, its spread. What its videos do; `how_to_shoot` \u2014 its reference hit step by step on that video's own clock, its length, what the format's videos keep and what a creator may make their own (where the format has a counted formula, `formula` lists what its breakouts do alike: each cue, how to do it, how widely in Shorti's words, and a breakout that shows it at a moment); `idea_card`, the format's own hook, turn and how a brand's product sits in it; its strongest hits with links and views (`why`: Shorti's line on a hit the format names as its own example); `moments`, what viewers reacted to and where; `flow`, how its way of shooting moved: what its newest breakouts did (`now`), its ladder of changes with how many took each rung in words, the worlds it moved into, up to three spots nobody has taken yet (`open`) and the same way of shooting under other sounds (`lineage`: its `id` for shorti_flow); `flow.spread` lists that lineage's observed platforms and elapsed days, with `flow.spread_line` in the answer's language (both absent for one platform); its page and the check with it filled. Address it by `format_id` (from shorti_what_to_shoot or shorti_find, or the slug of its page), or by `video_id` or `url` of one of its videos. The default summary keeps the shoot clock and keep/change, with three hits; detail='full' returns the unchanged legacy answer.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "detail": {
    "default": "summary",
    "description": "summary: compact agent answer, Korean person-facing text with lang=ko; model prompts are marked for_model=true. full: all compiled details, including original bilingual/model text.",
    "enum": [
     "summary",
     "full"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "format_id": {
    "anyOf": [
     {
      "maxLength": 120,
